question:
Hiring manager round for an SMTS backend role, framed as system design but with a Low Level Design focus: **design a food delivery app.** Topics that came up:

- core entities: user, restaurant, menu item, order, cart, delivery agent, payment;
- the **order state machine** (placed, confirmed, preparing, picked up, delivered or cancelled);
- delivery agent assignment using **geospatial indexing** (geohash versus quadtree), nearest-first versus load-balanced, and reassignment when an agent becomes unavailable;
- trade-offs: synchronous versus asynchronous confirmation, strong consistency for payments versus eventual consistency for delivery status, **push versus poll** for order tracking, **idempotent payment retries**, schema choices, menu caching;
- behavioral questions.
